# =====================================================================
#  ReportFailure.ab   ·   shared terminal behavior
# =====================================================================
#  reached by:   every `goto ReportFailure` in programs/
#
#  decision D4:  ReportFailure is COMPOSED.  it is not a primitive
#  and it is not a magic `throw`.  it is built out of the same
#  alphabet as everything else:
#
#       system report failure   ->  failure.report.ok | failed
#
#  that is the whole composition.  one step, one response, one halt.
#  the point is that the failure becomes a TERM in the trace like any
#  other term.  if the panel goes quiet after a bad delete, the trace
#  still shows that the failure was reported.
#
#  v4 equivalence:  none.  leftpanel_v4.html has no failure surface.
#                   commitEdit() silently restores the original name
#                   (line 538); moveNode() silently returns on all
#                   four of its guard branches (lines 616-623);
#                   copyPath() swallows the clipboard rejection with
#                   `.catch(() => {})` (line 793).
#
#  this is the first place where the machine is AHEAD of the build.
#  that is allowed and is recorded here rather than hidden: I7 says
#  the code must emit what the spec declares, and these emissions do
#  not exist yet.  they are specified, not built.

behavior ReportFailure

step system report failure
  catch failure.report.ok     halt
  catch failure.report.failed halt
